<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aulus Plautius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aulus Plautius was a Roman senator and general who commanded the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> ordered by the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> in 43 CE. Leading four legions, he defeated the Catuvellauni, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camulodunum">Camulodunum</a> with the emperor present, and accepted the surrender of peoples such as part of the Dobunni. He served as the first governor of the province of Britannia until 47 and was honoured with an ovation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aulus-plautius.jpg" alt="Aulus Plautius" width="320" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Piotr Stachiewicz (1858-1938) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stachiewicz-Aulus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
